WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.100
And when I went looking,

2
00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:03.460
I didn't find a sole body

3
00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:05.120
that had the concrete definition

4
00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:06.360
of an essential nutrient,

5
00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:07.800
or a sole body or organization

6
00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:09.280
that had a list of

7
00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:10.260
these are the essential ones

8
00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:11.810
and these are not the essential ones.

9
00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:13.630
So that in itself was interesting.

10
00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:15.280
All of the main sort of caveats

11
00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:16.100
boiled down to

12
00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:18.550
that the body needed the nutrient to survive.

13
00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:20.480
So it had to have a physiological function

14
00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:21.410
that was recognized.

15
00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:24.680
The body couldn't produce enough of that product

16
00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:26.670
of itself to service its own needs.

17
00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:27.900
So it did have to come

18
00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:29.090
from things like diet.

19
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:31.280
And then probably the more trickier one

20
00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:33.080
is that there had to be a certified

21
00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:35.720
or obvious deficiency state that could be reversed.

22
00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:37.750
So if you removed the nutrient,

23
00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:39.030
an illness occurred.

24
00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:40.570
So vitamin C and scurvy.

25
00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:42.770
And then when you returned the nutrient,

26
00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:44.750
the deficiency state went away.

27
00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:45.980
And that sort of framing

28
00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:47.040
makes a lot of sense

29
00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:48.680
for when most of the essential nutrients

30
00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:51.390
were discovered more than 50 years ago,

31
00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:53.440
where things like ethical concerns

32
00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:54.730
and trials weren't a problem.

33
00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:56.360
You could deprive people of nutrients

34
00:00:56.360 --> 00:00:57.310
and see what happened.

35
00:00:57.500 --> 00:00:58.800
Or there was natural situations

36
00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:00.680
such as the long sea voyages

37
00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:03.280
where people were without fruit and vegetables

38
00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:04.100
for months and months,

39
00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:05.940
where you'd naturally sort of observe

40
00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:08.630
deficiency states popping in for micronutrients.

41
00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:11.360
Those were the three sort of main criteria

42
00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:12.850
that we wanted to address.
